"""
tech_marketplace
=================

A small, self-contained Python toolkit that generates the
"Technology Analytics Marketplace" self-service report/dashboard
catalog as a single, offline-friendly HTML file.

Why this exists
----------------
The original artifact was a hand-written HTML file with inline CSS
and JavaScript. That is great for a one-off demo, but painful to
maintain: every rebrand (colors, logo, wording, icons) or every data
refresh (adding/removing dashboards) meant hand-editing markup.

This package turns that HTML file into a *template* driven by three
simple, swappable inputs:

1. ``AppConfig``  - branding, theme colors, icon glyphs, link/URL
   behavior and on-page copy (search placeholder, button labels,
   panel headings, etc).
2. ``Report`` records - the catalog of dashboards/reports to list,
   loadable from Python literals, JSON, or CSV.
3. A Jinja2 HTML template (``templates/marketplace.html.j2``) that
   renders both of the above into a polished, interactive, single
   file HTML page (search, filtering, hover previews, recommendation
   rail, all client-side, no server required).

Quick start
-----------
    from tech_marketplace import build_dashboard

    build_dashboard(output_path="dashboard.html")

Everything is customizable without touching the template or CSS -
see ``config.example.json`` and ``reports.example.json`` for the
full set of knobs, and README.md for a guided tour.
"""

from .models import Report, AppConfig
from .renderer import MarketplaceRenderer, build_dashboard
from .data_source import load_reports

__all__ = [
    "Report",
    "AppConfig",
    "MarketplaceRenderer",
    "build_dashboard",
    "load_reports",
]

__version__ = "1.0.0"
